/Title (LEGAL SINGULARITY IN INTERNATIONAL LAW)
/Author (Haarkon, Sleven)
/Subject (This paper develops the doctrine of Legal Singularity as a structural limit of international law, analyzing how treaty law under the Vienna Convention enables the collapse of juridical plurality and a systemic legal reset in response to global technological transformation.)
/Keywords (Legal Singularity, Juridical Singularity, International Law, Vienna Convention, VCLT, Treaty Law, State Succession, Lex Posterior, Territorial Scope, Network Infrastructure, Global Sovereignty, Jus Cogens, Customary International Law, International Organizations, ICJ Statute, Treaty Chains, Tacit Acceptance, Estoppel, Legal Theory, Global Governance, Legal Reset, Normative Collapse, Systemic Risk, Technological Singularity, Exponential Technology, Infrastructure Law, Sovereignty Theory, Public International Law, Legal Plurality, Normative Transformation)
>>
